/*
================================================================
 MEDRAS - AMBULANCE CONTROLLER
 FILE : 01_Ambulance.ino
 DEVICE: ESP32 #1
 ID    : AMB_001
================================================================

 FINAL RESPONSIBILITIES
 ----------------------------------------------------------------
 1. Receive emergency assignment from MEDRAS backend through MQTT.
 2. Loud/repeated emergency alert and 10-second response countdown.
 3. If no response, provide a SECOND 10-second response window.
 4. After second timeout, ask backend to reassign the emergency.
 5. Accept / Reject from physical buttons OR dashboard commands.
 6. After acceptance publish live GPS/data every second.
 7. Publish patient-location, pickup, hospital-arrival and completion events.
 8. Priority is allowed only when a patient is onboard.
 9. Priority activates BLE ambulance beacon.
10. Backend/junctions coordinate Green Corridor; junction uses BLE ~1 m.
11. Publish ETA/distance fields supplied by backend.
12. Publish SMS/call request/status information supplied by backend.
13. Automatically reconnect Wi-Fi and MQTT.
14. ESP32 device communication uses MQTT.
    Dashboards use HTTP/WebSocket through the backend.

 COMPONENTS USED
 ----------------------------------------------------------------
 1. ESP32 DevKit
 2. NEO-6M GPS Module
 3. SIM900A on this ambulance ESP32 can send SMS/place calls when the backend
    supplies the recipient number from its database. ESP32 #8 can remain a
    separate central gateway for other devices/workflows.
 4. 16x2 I2C LCD
 5. Buzzer
 6. Accept Push Button
 7. Reject Push Button
 8. Ambulance Priority Button
 9. Built-in ESP32 BLE (ambulance proximity beacon)
 10. Wi-Fi connectivity (ESP32 built-in)
 11. MQTT communication (ESP32 built-in Wi-Fi)
 12. SIM900A GSM module dedicated to this ambulance (separate suitable supply)
 13. Jumper wires and common GND

 LOCATION-LINK NOTIFICATION
 ----------------------------------------------------------------
 Every ambulance notification generated by this ESP32 includes:
 - A LIVE TRACKING LINK handled by the MEDRAS backend.
 - A CURRENT GPS LOCATION LINK using the ambulance coordinates.
 The backend/GSM Gateway should forward these links in SMS.
 Replace LIVE_TRACKING_BASE_URL with the real deployed MEDRAS
 tracking URL.

 FINAL AUDIT COVERAGE
 ----------------------------------------------------------------
 A. Emergency assignment + first 10-second alert       : COVERED
 B. Second 10-second alert window                     : COVERED
 C. Reassignment request after two timeouts            : COVERED
 D. Physical Accept / Reject                           : COVERED
 E. Dashboard Accept / Reject commands                 : COVERED
 F. Live GPS/data publication every 1 second            : COVERED
 G. Patient reached / pickup / hospital events          : COVERED
 H. Patient-onboard safety gate for priority            : COVERED
 I. Priority button + dashboard priority                : COVERED
 J. BLE ambulance beacon during priority                : COVERED
 K. Backend/junction Green Corridor coordination        : COVERED
 L. ETA and distance values from backend                : COVERED
 M. Backend-resolved local SIM900A SMS/calls             : ADDED (backend commands required)
 N. Location links in ambulance messages                : COVERED
 O. Wi-Fi and MQTT automatic reconnection               : COVERED
 P. LCD status + countdown                              : COVERED
 Q. GPS speed/satellites/HDOP                           : COVERED
 R. Hospital selected / hospital ready                  : COVERED
 S. Green Corridor active / stop / junction update      : COVERED
 T. Emergency cancel / complete                         : COVERED
 U. MQTT command/event telemetry                         : COVERED
 V. Dashboard live-tracking fields                      : COVERED
 W. Current Google Maps GPS snapshot link               : COVERED
 X. BLE beacon identity contains ambulance/emergency ID : COVERED
 Y. Backend remains responsible for routing, assignment,
    recipient resolution and dashboard WebSocket updates : BACKEND RESPONSIBILITY

 IMPORTANT GSM NOTE
 ----------------------------------------------------------------
 This version controls a separate SIM900A connected to ESP32 #1. The backend
 still owns all phone numbers: it resolves patient/family/hospital numbers
 from its database and sends GSM_SEND_SMS / GSM_CALL commands containing the
 selected number to this ambulance over authenticated MQTT. No phone number is
 hard-coded here. Configure the backend so these ambulance-local jobs are NOT
 also duplicated through ESP32 #8. ESP32 #8 may continue serving other devices.

 Vehicle and Patient/User notifications are generated by their own
 device/backend workflows. This ambulance file supplies the same
 location-link fields for all ambulance-originated notifications.
================================================================
*/

